<plain>
<text x="190.5" y="7.62" size="2.54" layer="94">Notes</text>
<text x="17.78" y="193.04" size="1.778" layer="94">The CPU initiates a read-modify-write cycle with a MEM_START pulse.</text>
<text x="17.78" y="187.96" size="1.778" layer="94">150 ns later MEM_BEGIN sets at the beginning of READ.</text>
<text x="17.78" y="182.88" size="1.778" layer="94">150 ns or more later STROBE is sent when the CPU should grab the READ data.</text>
<text x="17.78" y="172.72" size="1.778" layer="94">50 ns after TP2, INHIBIT begins.</text>
<text x="17.78" y="167.64" size="1.778" layer="94">100 ns after TP2, WRITE is asserted.</text>
<text x="17.78" y="162.56" size="1.778" layer="94">400 ns after WRITE begins, WRITE ends and MEM_DONE is sent to the CPU.</text>
<text x="17.78" y="177.8" size="1.778" layer="94">350 ns later, READ ends.</text>
